{"id":"dodo-v2-2021","slug":"dodo-v2-2021","sub":null,"name":"DODO V2 (DVM / Crowdpooling) init() exploit: two bots front-ran the real attacker, returned funds","date":"2021-03-08","one_liner":"Antelope, a generic flash-loan bot, replayed the DODO attacker's init() call at index 4 of block 12000022 and took 955,815 WSZO + 259,939 USDT; the attacker's tx at index 176 reverted. Antelope later returned most of its takes. Pre-Merge, in-block evidence only.","bot":"Antelope","race_type":"beat-pending-attack","narrative":"Bot 'Antelope' (EOA 0x3554187576ec..., contract 0x00000000e84f2bbd...) beat the real attacker 'Hippo' (EOA 0x368a6558255b...) in the SAME BLOCK on two pools: block 12000022 (bot index 4 @243 gwei vs attacker index 176 @132 gwei, attacker reverted) and block 12000102 (bot index 0 @1883 gwei vs attacker index 4 @600 gwei, attacker reverted). The bot's pool.init(...) payload is byte-identical (all 8 arguments, incl. the attacker's two fake tokens FDO/FUSDT) to the attacker's; the flashLoan amounts are the same 99%-of-balance figures (differ by 99 wei). Bot 'Cheetah' (EOA 0x8a14ce0f... via proxy 0xa57bd001...) then front-ran the attacker's two WITHDRAWALS from his 'bypass' contract 0x910fd17b: its inner call to the attacker's contract is calldata byte-identical to the attacker's own pending withdraw tx (blocks 12000167 and 12000171, bot indexes 1 / 3 vs attacker indexes 77 / 78), and won a gas war against Antelope (684.25 vs 652.17 gwei). Pre-Merge: in-block evidence only; no mempool archive. Ordering is by gas price in a public gas war; no coinbase payments in any tx.","chain":"ethereum","verdict":"confirmed-onchain","t0_ms":1615235143000,"pre_merge":true,"premerge_note":"Pre-Merge: no relays/slots. Flashbots MEV-geth bundles. blocks.flashbots.net answers HTTP 410 (decommissioned); bundle membership below is INFERRED (`inferred_bundle_like`) from coinbase transfers + gas price, not authoritative.","slot":null,"block":{"number":12000022,"hash":"0x5cf9c78d930